<title>UK: Birmingham Airport passenger figures down in Sept..</title>
<headline>Birmingham Airport passenger figures down in Sept..</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Birmingham International Airport said on Monday that it handled 588,655 passengers in September, 1.3 percent lower than a year ago.</p>
<p>It blamed the fall in total passengers on continued weakness in the charter holiday sector.</p>
<p>Scheduled traffic rose 4.4 percent, while the charter sector fell 7.4 percent compared with September 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
